# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the fuzz targets (LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=fuzz/lsan.supp).
#
# The ZSTD / zlib codecs cache one context per thread in pthread TSD
# (src/compression/zstd.c, gzip.c) and free it from the key destructor when the
# thread exits. OpenMP pool threads outlive a single fuzz input, and on macOS
# LeakSanitizer does not scan the pthread TSD of live threads, so the first
# input that decompresses on each worker thread is reported as a leak. The
# contexts are bounded (one per thread) and still referenced; not a leak.
leak:get_dctx
leak:get_cctx
leak:gzip_tls_get
leak:inflateInit2_
leak:deflateInit2_
